                <pb facs="0106" n="96" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg96"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/734: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sparks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-08T11:00:00-05:00">December 8, 1941—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:09 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>241. President Lescot with the unanimous approval of the permanent Committee of
                    National Assembly declared war on Japan.</p>
                <p>A state of siege has been declared and warning has been served that any saboteur
                    will be tried by court martial and executed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sparks</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
